# TrueTalk.Ai Development Files Guide

This document lists **only the files we modified or created** during this development session. It explains exactly where they are and what specific features they handle.

---

## 🖥️ BACKEND (Django)
**Base Folder:** `TrueTalk.Ai/ChatRoom/`

### 📂 `ChatRoom/` (The Core Logic)

| File | Exact Path | What We Did & Why |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **[models.py](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Documents/GitHub/TrueTalk.Ai/ChatRoom/models.py)** | [ChatRoom/models.py](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Documents/GitHub/TrueTalk.Ai/ChatRoom/models.py) | **Database Schema**<br>- Added [Group](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Documents/GitHub/TrueTalk.Ai/ChatRoom/models.py#5-15) model for group chats.<br>- Updated [Message](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Documents/GitHub/TrueTalk.Ai/ChatRoom/models.py#17-53) model with `is_read` (for blue ticks), `msg_type` (text/image/video), and `attachment_url`. |
| **[consumers.py](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Documents/GitHub/TrueTalk.Ai/ChatRoom/consumers.py)** | [ChatRoom/consumers.py](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Documents/GitHub/TrueTalk.Ai/ChatRoom/consumers.py) | **Real-Time Logic (WebSockets)**<br>- Updated [ChatConsumer](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Documents/GitHub/TrueTalk.Ai/ChatRoom/consumers.py#8-171) to handle [read_receipt](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Documents/GitHub/TrueTalk.Ai/ChatRoom/consumers.py#111-117) events.<br>- Added logic to broadcast messages to specific Groups or Users.<br>- Handles saving messages to the DB automatically. |
| **[views.py](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Documents/GitHub/TrueTalk.Ai/ChatRoom/views.py)** | [ChatRoom/views.py](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Documents/GitHub/TrueTalk.Ai/ChatRoom/views.py) | **API Endpoints**<br>- Created [UserViewSet](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Documents/GitHub/TrueTalk.Ai/ChatRoom/views.py#19-33) to auto-create users on login.<br>- Created [GroupViewSet](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Documents/GitHub/TrueTalk.Ai/ChatRoom/views.py#14-17) to create and list groups.<br>- Created [MessageViewSet](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Documents/GitHub/TrueTalk.Ai/ChatRoom/views.py#9-12) to fetch chat history. |
| **[serializers.py](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Documents/GitHub/TrueTalk.Ai/ChatRoom/serializers.py)** | [ChatRoom/serializers.py](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Documents/GitHub/TrueTalk.Ai/ChatRoom/serializers.py) | **Data Formatting**<br>- Updated [MessageSerializer](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Documents/GitHub/TrueTalk.Ai/ChatRoom/serializers.py#17-99) to include the new fields (`is_read`, `attachment_url`).<br>- Created [GroupSerializer](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Documents/GitHub/TrueTalk.Ai/ChatRoom/serializers.py#11-15) to send group member data to the frontend. |
| **[urls.py](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Documents/GitHub/TrueTalk.Ai/ChatRoom/urls.py)** | [ChatRoom/urls.py](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Documents/GitHub/TrueTalk.Ai/ChatRoom/urls.py) | **API Routing**<br>- Registered the new routes: `/api/chat/users/`, `/api/chat/groups/`, etc. |

